Not linked into ~/.claude/skills/ by default, and /sync-config leaves it alone.

This skill does a job that happens once per machine — migrating ~/.aws/config to sso-session
blocks. Carrying it in the always-loaded skill list for the rest of time costs trigger surface
for no benefit, so it gets linked for the migration and unlinked afterwards. Run these from the
primary clone, not a worktree — a link into a worktree dangles as soon as the worktree is removed:

  ln -s "$PWD/aws-sso-sessions" ~/.claude/skills/aws-sso-sessions
  rm ~/.claude/skills/aws-sso-sessions

The link is only visible to the Skill tool after one Claude Code restart, since it is a new
directory under ~/.claude/skills/ rather than an edit to an already-linked target.

Any skill directory carrying this marker is treated the same way.
